[38;5;231m⏺[39m This one is a one-line edit, but session lifetime is a security control, so I want your explicit go-ahead before
  touching it.

  The change: [38;5;153mconfig.js:3[39m, [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30[39m → [38;5;153m480[39m.

  The consequence: an idle or abandoned session stays valid 16× longer. A session token stolen from a shared machine, an
  unattended browser, a stale cookie, or logs has an 8-hour window to be replayed instead of 30 minutes, and users who
  walk away stay logged in for a full workday. [38;5;153mserver.js:3[39m is the only consumer, so nothing else in the repo breaks —
  the risk is entirely the auth-window widening, not the code.

